instagram came out of one wanting to be  my own boss i was like you know what i  want to work for myself i want to work  on ideas i really hope i'm going to make  money this is kevin systrom in 2010 he  launched instagram three years later he  sold it to facebook for one billion  dollars  but instagram nearly didn't happen his  first app was a complete disaster and  only had about a hundred active users  after its launch until one day during a  conversation with his wife he had an  epiphany that changed the course of his  life he went on to build one of the most  popular social media apps and became a  billionaire  this is the story of how a single reply  sparked the idea for a hundred billion  dollar company  kevin was born on december 30th 1983. he  grew up in holliston massachusetts a  wealthy suburb of boston during high  school kevin was introduced to computer  programming his interest grew from  playing doom 2 and he even created his  own levels as a teenager kevin was  obsessed with record collecting and  djing while still in high school he used  to have his friends sneak him into  nightclubs in the boston area open for  established djs  kevin applied to stanford university he  had planned to study computer science  but once he arrived he decided to switch  majors to management science and  engineering  kevin soon became interested in  photography during his junior year he  spent a semester in florence a city in  central italy to study photography it  was in florence that kevin stumbled upon  the aesthetic that would define  instagram in the early days one of his  professors showed him a cheap film  camera called a holger which takes hip  vintage looking photos  right before his senior year at stanford  kevin interned at a podcasting company  called odio odio was founded by evan  williams who went on to create twitter  twitter ceo jack dorsey was also working  at odeo at the time and he and kevin  became good friends in 2004 while kevin  was still in college he met facebook ceo  mark zuckerberg he tried to recruit him  to work for facebook but kevin thought  facebook was just a fad and turned him  down after graduation kevin was offered  a job at google after three years at  google kevin left to work at a social  travel recommendation startup called  nextstop  around the same time kevin began working  on his own app which he initially named  bourbon after his favorite spirit the  app combined location-based social  networking and photo sharing he made the  prototype of the app and pitched it to  baseline ventures and andreessen  horowitz during a party after the first  meeting he decided to quit his job in  order to work on bourbon full-time  within two weeks of quitting his job he  received a five hundred thousand dollar  seed funding round from both baseline  ventures and andreessen horowitz soon  after kevin brought on mike krieger as a  co-founder mike also graduated from  stanford just two years behind kevin  soon after mike joined the pair decided  to focus on bourbon  on its launch the app completely tanked  bourbon only had around a hundred active  users most users who tried the app said  it was far too complicated and did too  much kevin and mike's first venture  together was a complete disaster  instead of trying to fix the issues of  bourbon they pivoted kevin and mike  decided to ditch bourbon and instead  focused on building a photo sharing app  back then photo sharing apps were  already quite common but there wasn't an  app that allowed users to post great  looking photos for their followers kevin  and mike were working on their app until  one day while kevin was walking along  the beach with his wife he asked his  wife whether she was interested in his  photo sharing app but his wife said that  she wasn't interested kevin said that  his friends used filters on their photos  so she just replied well you should  probably have filters then  her reply went on to change his life  on that same day kevin went home to his  computer and started to make the first  ever instagram filter called x pro 2 it  is still used in the app today  in october 2010 kevin and mike  officially changed the name to instagram  the name was a combination of instant  and telegram  when the app went live more than 25 000  people downloaded it in the first 24  hours crashing instagram servers even  celebrities like kim kardashian justin  bieber and beyonce started using the app  in 2012 facebook had been in months of  turmoil and scandals mark zuckerberg  even saw instagram as a threat to  facebook so in april 2012 mark  zuckerberg and facebook acquired  instagram for one billion dollars going  into the deal kevin owned 40 of  instagram so he made an estimated 400  million dollars from the sale after  facebook's acquisition of instagram the  app was continuously being developed and  improved upon  instagram added more and more features  for its users the app continued its  success as it gained more users year  after year it also started to become one  of facebook's biggest revenue drivers as  its popularity increased however in 2017  instagram was accused on multiple  occasions of copying various new  functions from its closest competitor  snapchat regarding the issue kevin  argued that all new apps launched by  tech companies nowadays are remixes of  existing apps and all ideas are original  when you remix them and bring your own  flavor despite instagram's success  however there were reportedly growing  tensions with mark zuckerberg over the  direction of the app  instagram's autonomy began to crumble  then in september 2018 kevin and mike  abruptly announced that they were  stepping down as ceo and cto  respectively after leaving instagram  kevin and mike kept a low profile though  they did attend a few conferences in  2019  kevin has been quiet on instagram too he  has since deleted all the photos he  posted on the app over the past couple  of years  today instagram is still one of the most  popular social media apps in the world  with over 1 billion active monthly users  instagram is one of facebook's most  valuable assets in 2020 instagram  generated an estimated 24 billion  dollars in revenue nowadays instagram  has a valuation of a hundred billion  dollars  [Music]  these days kevin is worth an estimated  1.7 billion dollars he's recently been  involved in the fashion industry and has  met and worked with several well-known  designers he's also attended the mech  gala multiple times kevin took a failed  app and turned it into one of the most  popular social media apps in the world  he managed to build a company and sell  it for one billion dollars in just three  short years  there's a lesson in every story what can  we learn from kevin's journey to success  instead of persevering with bourbon  kevin decided to pivot  that became the single most important  decision he ever made with his company a  pivot is fundamentally changing the  direction of a business when you realize  the current products or services aren't  meeting the needs of the market  kevin recognized that the market didn't  want all the complicated features such  as bookings and point systems  but instead wanted a simple app that  allowed users to share good looking  photos with their followers  so he pivoted  a big part of entrepreneurship is the  ability to solve problems kevin  identified a problem in the market at  the time there wasn't an app that  allowed people to add filters to photos  to share with their followers so he  created an app that solved the problem  and was massively rewarded  ultimately making him incredibly rich  and successful what do you guys think  was he a brilliant developer who  revolutionized the industry or did he  just rip off other apps the comment  section in this one will be very  interesting thanks for staying till the  end of this video if you enjoyed this  video then be sure to hit the like  button drop a comment subscribe and hit  the notification bell for more content  like this also be sure to check out our  other videos on this channel links are  in the description and we'll see you in  the next one
 

